        q: 'What is Delta Lake and what problems does it solve?',
        a: 'Delta Lake is an open-source storage layer that adds ACID transactions, schema enforcement, time travel, and upsert (MERGE) capabilities on top of Parquet files in a data lake. It solves: small file problems, partial write failures, schema drift, and the inability to update/delete in plain data lakes.',
        detailedAnswer: 'Without Delta Lake, a Parquet data lake has no atomicity — a partial write leaves corrupt data. Delta\'s transaction log (_delta_log/) records every operation as a JSON commit file. Readers always see the latest committed snapshot. `VACUUM RETAIN 7 DAYS` cleans old files while preserving time travel. Open format: Delta tables are just Parquet + JSON logs — readable by Spark, Trino, DuckDB.',
