        q: 'What is the difference between a Fabric Lakehouse and a Fabric Warehouse?',
        a: 'Lakehouse stores data as Delta Parquet files accessible via Spark notebooks and a read-only SQL Analytics Endpoint. Warehouse is a full T-SQL engine with DML (INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE), stored procedures, and concurrent SQL access. Use Lakehouse for Spark-heavy ETL and Bronze/Silver data; use Warehouse for Gold-layer SQL-first transformations and concurrent analyst workloads.',
        detailedAnswer: 'Key differences: (1) Format — Lakehouse uses Delta format (ACID, time travel, OPTIMIZE). Warehouse uses its own internal format — no Delta time travel. (2) Write operations — Lakehouse writes via Spark; SQL Analytics Endpoint is read-only. Warehouse supports full DML from SQL. (3) Concurrency — Warehouse is optimized for many concurrent SQL users. Lakehouse SQL endpoint can bottleneck under heavy concurrency. (4) Power BI — both support Direct Lake, but Warehouse tables need to be surfaced via a Semantic Model. (5) Cross-query — you can JOIN Warehouse tables to Lakehouse tables via the SQL Analytics Endpoint cross-database query. Production pattern: Bronze/Silver in Lakehouse (Spark), Gold in Warehouse (SQL SCD logic, dimension tables).',
