        q: 'What is Direct Lake mode in Power BI and when does it fall back to DirectQuery?',
        a: 'Direct Lake reads Delta Parquet files directly from OneLake into Power BI — no data import, no scheduled refresh. It is as fast as Import mode because column data is loaded into the VertiPaq engine on demand. It falls back to DirectQuery when queries exceed the framing threshold (too many distinct values loaded), when tables are in a Warehouse (not Delta format), or when the data model requires relationships Direct Lake cannot resolve.',
        detailedAnswer: 'Framing: Direct Lake pre-loads column metadata (a "frame") without loading all data. When a query exceeds the frame (too many rows or distinct values for the engine to cache), it automatically falls back to DirectQuery against the SQL Analytics Endpoint — slower but still correct. To avoid fallback: OPTIMIZE Delta tables regularly to reduce file count, use ZORDER on high-cardinality columns used in filters, and partition by the most common filter dimension (date). Monitoring: Power BI Performance Analyzer shows when Direct Lake frames are hit vs. DirectQuery fallback. Production checklist before Direct Lake: run OPTIMIZE on all tables, confirm Delta table has statistics, verify row count is within Direct Lake capacity limits for your F-SKU.',
